---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import { WHEREBY_PRIVACY_URL, WHEREBY_COOKIES_URL } from "../config/training";

// Both optional external services are click-to-load. Keep this notice aligned
// with their facades, src/scripts/training.ts and public/_headers.
const lastUpdated = "1 October 2026";
---

<Base
  title="Cookies Policy — Fleetlix"
  description="Cookie use on fleetlix.com, including Cloudflare security cookies and the optional, click-to-load walkthrough video and Whereby training room."
>
  <Header />
  <main class="bg-[color:var(--color-offwhite)]">
    <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16 md:py-24">
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.18em] uppercase text-[color:var(--color-amber)]">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 font-[family-name:var(--font-display)] font-extrabold text-4xl md:text-5xl tracking-tight text-[color:var(--color-graphite)]">
        Cookies Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-[color:var(--color-slate)]">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <div class="mt-10 space-y-8 text-[color:var(--color-slate)] leading-relaxed">
        <section>
          <h2 class="font-[family-name:var(--font-display)] font-bold text-2xl text-[color:var(--color-graphite)]">1. What this page covers</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            This page explains how cookies and similar storage technologies are used on the Fleetlix marketing website (<a href="https://fleetlix.com" class="underline hover:text-[color:var(--color-graphite)]">fleetlix.com</a>). It complements our <a href="/privacy" class="underline hover:text-[color:var(--color-graphite)]">Privacy Policy</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-[family-name:var(--font-display)] font-bold text-2xl text-[color:var(--color-graphite)]">2. What cookies are</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            A cookie is a small text file that a website asks your browser to store on your device. Cookies are widely used to make websites work, to remember preferences, and (less benignly) to track people across sites for advertising. Under UK law — the Privacy and Electronic Communications Regulations (PECR), as supplemented by UK GDPR — non-essential cookies require your consent. Strictly necessary cookies, used to deliver a service you have asked for, do not.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-[family-name:var(--font-display)] font-bold text-2xl text-[color:var(--color-graphite)]">3. Cookies used on this website</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            <strong>Fleetlix sets no first-party cookies on this marketing site.</strong> We do not install analytics, marketing, advertising, or behavioural-tracking cookies. There is no Google Analytics, no Meta Pixel, no LinkedIn Insight Tag, no advertising network, and no third-party widget, chat box, or social embed that loads on its own. The optional training service has its own cookie practices, described below.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Two optional features contact external providers: the walkthrough video, fetched from Supabase Storage <em>only if you press play</em>, and the Whereby training room, loaded <em>only if you choose to enter</em>. They are covered in sections 4 and 5 below.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Our hosting provider, Cloudflare, may set a small number of <em>strictly necessary</em> cookies for site security and bot management when their protection services are active:
          </p>
          <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="w-full text-sm border border-[color:var(--color-mist)] rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
              <thead class="bg-[color:var(--color-mist)]/40 text-left text-[color:var(--color-graphite)]">
                <tr>
                  <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Cookie</th>
                  <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Set by</th>
                  <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Purpose</th>
                  <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Lifetime</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody class="divide-y divide-[color:var(--color-mist)]">
                <tr>
                  <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top"><code>__cf_bm</code></td>
                  <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top">Cloudflare</td>
                  <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top">Distinguishes humans from bots to protect the site against malicious automated traffic. Strictly necessary; not used for tracking or advertising.</td>
                  <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top">30 minutes</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top"><code>cf_clearance</code></td>
                  <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top">Cloudflare</td>
                  <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top">Records that a visitor has successfully passed a Cloudflare security challenge, so they aren't repeatedly challenged. Strictly necessary.</td>
                  <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top">Up to 1 year</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm">
            Cloudflare's full list of cookies and their privacy practices is documented at <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/fundamentals/reference/policies-compliances/cloudflare-cookies/" class="underline hover:text-[color:var(--color-graphite)]" rel="noopener" target="_blank">developers.cloudflare.com/fundamentals/reference/policies-compliances/cloudflare-cookies</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-[family-name:var(--font-display)] font-bold text-2xl text-[color:var(--color-graphite)]">4. The walkthrough video</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            The product walkthrough video on our <a href="/walkthrough" class="underline hover:text-[color:var(--color-graphite)]">walkthrough page</a> is served from another address. It is a plain video file stored in <strong>Supabase Storage</strong>, which is the same infrastructure provider that runs the Fleetlix application. It is played by your browser's own built-in video player — there is <strong>no third-party video service, no embedded player, and no third-party JavaScript running on the walkthrough page</strong>.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            <strong>Nothing is requested until you press play.</strong> Until you do, the page shows a still image served from this website, and your browser does not contact Supabase at all — nothing is sent, nothing is stored, and no cookie is set. This is a deliberate design choice, not a side effect: pressing play is how you consent to loading it.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            If you press play, your browser requests the video file. At that point Supabase receives your IP address and browser information, as an unavoidable part of sending you a file, and its content delivery network (Cloudflare) sets one strictly-necessary bot-management cookie, <code>__cf_bm</code>, on the <code>supabase.co</code> domain. That cookie protects the file from automated abuse, lasts 30 minutes, and is not used for advertising or to track you across websites. No profile is built, and we receive nothing that identifies you personally. Supabase's privacy practices are set out at <a href="https://supabase.com/privacy" class="underline hover:text-[color:var(--color-graphite)]" rel="noopener" target="_blank">supabase.com/privacy</a>.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            If you would rather not load it at all, simply don't press play — the chapter list on that page describes what the video covers section by section, and everything else on the site works without it.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="training">
          <h2 class="font-[family-name:var(--font-display)] font-bold text-2xl text-[color:var(--color-graphite)]">5. Live training sessions</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Our <a href="/training" class="underline hover:text-[color:var(--color-graphite)]">training page</a> offers an optional video room provided by <strong>Whereby</strong>. The room is blocked until you choose <strong>Enter training room</strong>, beside a notice explaining that you are loading Whereby's service and cookies. Visiting the page alone does not contact Whereby. You can also choose to open the room directly on Whereby's website.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Once you choose to enter, Whereby receives technical information such as your IP address and browser details and runs its own service inside the room. It may use cookies and similar storage for service operation, preferences and its own analytics. Whereby's <a href={WHEREBY_COOKIES_URL} class="underline hover:text-[color:var(--color-graphite)]" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cookie Policy</a> describes its cookies, purposes, durations and available choices; its <a href={WHEREBY_PRIVACY_URL} class="underline hover:text-[color:var(--color-graphite)]" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Privacy Policy</a> explains how it handles personal information. These practices are separate from Fleetlix's marketing website.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Your browser separately controls camera and microphone permission. Use <strong>Close room</strong> to unload the embedded service, or close the separate tab if you opened it directly. This stops the room loading further content; it does not remove cookies or information already sent to Whereby. You can manage stored cookies through your browser settings. To avoid the service entirely, leave the room unopened.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-[family-name:var(--font-display)] font-bold text-2xl text-[color:var(--color-graphite)]">6. How we ask before loading optional content</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            The marketing pages do not automatically load analytics, marketing or advertising cookies. Optional external content stays unloaded until you make a choice on the relevant page.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            The walkthrough uses an explicit play button. The training room uses an explicit entry button with a privacy and cookie notice. Neither choice is saved: if you revisit the page, the external content remains blocked until you choose again. Visitors who leave these features unopened do not contact either provider.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            If that changes — for example, if we add product analytics, or any embed that loads without being clicked — we will introduce a proper consent mechanism and update this page before anything is set.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-[family-name:var(--font-display)] font-bold text-2xl text-[color:var(--color-graphite)]">7. Managing cookies in your browser</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            You can block or delete cookies through your browser settings. Blocking strictly necessary cookies may prevent parts of the site from working as intended — for example, you may be repeatedly shown a security challenge. Instructions for the major browsers:
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 list-disc pl-6">
            <li><a href="https://support.google.com/chrome/answer/95647" class="underline hover:text-[color:var(--color-graphite)]" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Google Chrome</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://support.apple.com/guide/safari/manage-cookies-sfri11471/mac" class="underline hover:text-[color:var(--color-graphite)]" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Apple Safari</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/cookies-information-websites-store-on-your-computer" class="underline hover:text-[color:var(--color-graphite)]" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Mozilla Firefox</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-edge/delete-cookies-in-microsoft-edge-63947406-40ac-c3b8-57b9-2a946a29ae09" class="underline hover:text-[color:var(--color-graphite)]" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Microsoft Edge</a></li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-[family-name:var(--font-display)] font-bold text-2xl text-[color:var(--color-graphite)]">8. Changes to this policy</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We will update this page if our use of cookies changes. The "Last updated" date above always reflects the most recent revision.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-[family-name:var(--font-display)] font-bold text-2xl text-[color:var(--color-graphite)]">9. Contact</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Questions about cookies or anything else in this policy? Email <a href="mailto:contact@fleetlix.com" class="underline hover:text-[color:var(--color-graphite)]">contact@fleetlix.com</a>.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</Base>
